# DURABLE REPRO — `.map()` on `Option[String]` (the string-coercion bail path)
# still corrupts the receiver even AFTER the Round XIV combinator-receiver
# class-fix (74f566c6). The adapter BAILS to the C-inline fallback path via
# `has_string_coercion` (methods.rs L3517-3527) BEFORE reaching the fixed
# scrut_local materialization — the fallback has its own clone site at
# methods.rs ~L2020-2053 with distinct `!is_last_use` semantics.
#
# WRONG (POST-FIX at 74f566c6+):
#   `gg build`: succeeds
#   binary exit=1, prints:
#     gorget: panic: gorget_string_free invariant: cap=281473324163072 but alloc=NULL
#     hi
#   The `hi` line is the receiver readback; then a heap-corruption panic fires
#   at cleanup. So the receiver IS still there, but the ownership hand-off is
#   producing a torn/aliased String value that fails validation.
#
# INTENDED: prints `2` (mapped length) then `hi` (receiver preserved), exit 0.
#
# CLASS: string-coercion combinator fallback path shares receiver-ownership
# class. Not shipped in Round XIV (REV-P2 RSV-10 clarification: skip mirror,
# file TODO, keep landing rest of class-fix). Filed under §CoW > ### High in
# TODO.md for a follow-up round with its own scout + design.

void call_it(Option[String] p):
    Option[int] r = p.map((String s): s.len())
    if r is Some(v):
        print(v)
    if p is Some(s2):
        print(s2)

void main():
    call_it(Some("hi"))
